- If the partner is β thalassaemia carrier (β/β-), the fetus has a 50% chance of haemoglobin S/β- thalassemia and a 50% chance of β thalassemia trait.  
- If the partner is haemoglobin S carrier (β/S), the fetus has a 50% chance of sickle cell anaemia (SS) and a 50% chance of haemoglobin S trait (β/S).  
