   \[ \text{H(C}_7\text{H}_5\text{O}_2\text{) (s)} + \text{NaOH (aq)} \rightarrow \text{H}_2\text{O (l)} + \text{H}_2\text{CO}_3\text{ (aq)} + \text{Na}^+\text{ (aq)} \]  
   This equation shows the balanced reaction between solid benzoic acid and sodium hydroxide, producing water, carbonic acid, and sodium ions.  

2. **Observable Effects:**  
   - **Heat Generation (Exothermic Reaction):** The reaction is exothermic, meaning it releases heat.  
   - **Temperature Increase:** If the reaction is conducted in a solution, the temperature of the solution will increase.  
   - **Dissolution:** The solid benzoic acid will dissolve in the solution as it reacts with the sodium hydroxide.  
   - **Formation of a Precipitate:** The reaction produces carbonic acid, which is unstable and decomposes into water and carbon dioxide.  
