In practice, the optimal concentration and duration of exposure will depend on the specific reaction and the conditions of the reaction. For example, in photodynamic therapy, the concentration of the photosensitizer and the duration of exposure will be determined by the need to balance the effectiveness of the treatment with the potential for side effects.

