   The balanced equation shows that 1 mole of propane (C3H8) releases 2220 kJ of heat when burned.  

2. **Calculate the total heat released:**  
   Since you have 2.5 moles of propane, multiply the moles by the enthalpy change per mole:  
   \[
   \text{Heat released} = 2.5 \text{ mol} \times -2220 \text{ kJ/mol} = -5550 \text{ kJ}
   \]  

3. **Interpret the sign:**  
   The negative sign indicates that heat is released (exothermic reaction).  

