Thus, \(a - b = 10k_3\), which means \(a \equiv b \pmod{10}\).

Thus, if \(a \equiv b \pmod{2}\) and \(a \equiv b \pmod{5}\), then \(a \equiv b \pmod{10}\).

Combining the two cases, we find that \(a \equiv b \pmod{10}\), if and only if \(a \equiv b \pmod{2}\) and \(a \equiv b \pmod{5}\).

