","The study types are as follows:  

a) **Retrospective**. The study looks backward in time to examine past smoking habits (e.g., ""if they smoked in the past"") to see if they are associated with current cancer status.  
b) **Cross-sectional**. The survey collects data on eating habits and health at a single point in time.  
c) **Prospective**. The study follows a group of people forward in time, tracking their behaviors (eating/exercise) and observing who develops cancer later.  
d) **Cross-sectional**. The study compares prices at a single point in time.  

**Key Differences:**  
- **Cross-sectional**: Data collected at one specific time.  
- **Retrospective**: Looks backward in time to examine past events.  
- **Prospective**: Follows subjects forward in time to observe future outcomes.  

$\boxed{\text{The study types are as follows:  
a) Retrospective.  
b) Cross-sectional.  
