","To calculate the activation energy \( E_a \), we use the Arrhenius equation:
\[
\frac{k_2}{k_1} = \frac{A_2 e^{-\frac{E_a}{RT_2}}}{A_1 e^{-\frac{E_1}{RT_1}}} = \frac{A_2}{A_1} e^{-\frac{E_a}{R} \left \frac{1}{T_2} - \frac{1}{T_1} \right]}
\]
Since the pre-exponential factors \( A \) are assumed to be the same, we can simplify the equation to:
\[
\frac{k_2}{k_1} = e^{-\frac{E_a}{R} \left \frac{1}{T_2} - \frac{1}{T_1} \right]}
\]
Taking the natural logarithm of both sides:
\[
\ln \left( \frac{k_2}{k_1} \right) = -\frac{E_a}{R} \left \frac{1}{T_2} - \frac{1}{T_1} \right]
\]
Rearranging to solve for \( E_a \):
\[
\frac{E_a}{R} = -\frac{1}{R} \ln \left \frac{k_2}{k_1} \right] \left \frac{1}{T_2} - \frac{1}{T_1} \right]
\]
\[
E_a = - R \ln \left \frac{k_2}{k_1} \right] \left \frac{1}{T_2} - \frac{1}{T_1} \right]
\]

Substitute the given values:
\[
k_1 = 10^{-1} \, \text{M}^{-1} \text{s}^{-1} \\
k_2 = 10^4 \, \text{M}^{-1} \text{s}^{-1} \\
T_1 = 1000 \, \text{K} \\
T_2 = 1000 / 0.0012 = 833.3 \, \text{K} \\
R = 2 \, \text{cal K}^{-1} \text{mol}^{-1}
