\[
\Delta E \geq \frac{h}{2\tau}
\]

where \(h\) is Planck's constant (\(6.635 \times 10^{-34} \text{ eV s}\)).

Substituting the given lifetime \(\tau = 2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s}\):

\[
\Delta E \geq \frac{6.635 \times 10^{-34} \text{ eV s}}{2 \times 2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s}} = 1.65875 \times 10^{-11} \text{ eV}
\]

