\]

Thus, the uncertainty in the rest energy is approximately \(8.4 \times 10^{-15} \text{ MeV}\).

The typical range of outcomes for measurements of the Σ⁺ rest energy would be:

\[
1385 \text{ MeV} \pm 8.4 \times 10^{-15} \text{ MeV}
\]

Since the uncertainty is very small compared to the rest energy, the measurement is very precise.

