   \[
   m_{gas} = \frac{\Delta H_{gas}}{c_p (T_1 - T_2)} = \frac{1858.5 \text{ kJ}}{1.005 \text{ kJ/kg K} \times (1373 - 873)} = \frac{1858.5}{1005 \times 500} = 0.377 \text{ kg}
   \]  
   The entropy change of the gas is:  
   \[
   \Delta S_{gas} = m_{gas} c_p \ln\left(\frac{T_1}{T_2}\right) = 0.377 \text{ kg} \times 1.005 \text{ kJ/kg K} \times \ln\left(\frac{1373}{873}\right) = 0.377 \times 1.005 \times 0.525 = 0.200 \text{ kJ/K}
   \]  

2. **Entropy change of the water (\(\Delta S_{water}\)):**  
   The water vaporizes at constant temperature, so the entropy change is:  
