The discrete diffusion equation is given by:
\[
\phi_j^{n+1} = \phi_j^{n-1} + \frac{2\kappa \Delta t}{(\Delta x)^2} \left( \phi_{j+1}^n - \phi_j_{n} - \phi_j_{n-1} + \phi_{j-1}^n \right).
\]
Rearranging the equation, we get:
\[
\phi_j^{n+1} + \frac{\2\kappa \Delta t}{(\Delta x})^2 \phi_j^n = \frac{2\kappa \Delta t}{(\Delta x})^2 \phi_{j+1}^n + \frac{2\kappa \Delta t}{(\Delta x})^2 \phi_{j-1}^n + \frac{2\kappa \Delta t}{(\Delta x})^2 \phi_j_{n-1}.
\]
Let \(\lambda = \frac{2\kappa \Delta t}{(\Delta x)^2}\). Then the equation becomes:
\[
\phi_j^{n+1} + \lambda \phi_j^n = \lambda \phi_{j+1}^n + \lambda \phi_{j-1}^n + \lambda \phi_j_{n-1}.
\]
Solving for \(\phi_{j+1}^n\):
\[
\lambda \phi_{j+1}^n = \phi_{j+1}^{n+1} + \lambda \phi_j^n - \lambda \phi_{j-1}^n - \lambda \phi_{j-1}^n.
\]
\[
\phi_{j+1}^n = \frac{\phi_{j+1}^{n+1} + \lambda \phi_j^n - \lambda \phi_{j-1}^n - \lambda \phi_{j-1}^n}{\lambda}.
\]
This is not useful for stability analysis. Instead, we consider the diffusion equation in terms of the time derivative:
\[
\frac{\phi_{j}^n - \phi_j_{n-1}}{\Delta t} = \kappa \frac{\partial^2 \phi_j}{\partial x^2}.
