\[
\mathbf{V} = \mathbf{V}_x \mathbf{i} + \mathbf{V}_y \mathbf{j} + 0 \mathbf{k}.
\]
The cross product is given by:
\[
\mathbf{V} \times \mathbf{j} = \mathbf{k} \cdot \left(\mathbf{V}_x \mathbf{i} + \mathbf{V}_y \mathbf{j} + 0 \mathbf{k}\right) = \mathbf{V}_x \mathbf{k} \times \mathbf{i} + \mathbf{V}_y \mathbf{k} \times \mathbf{j} + 0 \mathbf{k} \times \mathbf{k}.
\]
Since \(\mathbf{k} \times \mathbf{i} = \mathbf{j}\), \(\mathbf{k} \times \mathbf{j} = -\mathbf{i}\), and \(\mathbf{k} \times \mathbf{k} = 0\), we have:
\[
\mathbf{V} \times \mathbf{j} = \mathbf{V}_x \mathbf{j} - \mathbf{V}_y \mathbf{i}.
\]
Thus, the cross product is:
\[
\mathbf{V} \times \mathbf{j} = - \mathbf{V}_y \mathbf{i} + \mathbf{V}_x \mathbf{j}.
\]
The cross product is given by the cross product of the unit vectors \(\mathbf{i}\), \(\mathbf{j}\), and \(\mathbf{k}\) with the components of the vector field:
\[
\text{curl} \ \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \mathbf{V}_x - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \mathbf{V}_y \times \mathbf{j}.
\]
Thus, the components of the curl are:
\[
\text{curl} \ \mathbf{V} = \left(\frac{\partial}{\partial y} \mathbf{V}_x - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \mathbf{V}_y\right) \times \mathbf{j} = \left(\frac{\partial}{\partial y} \mathbf{V}_x - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \mathbf{V}_y\right].
\]
The components of the cross product are:
\[
\text{curl} \ \mathbf{V} = \left(\frac{\partial}{\partial y} \mathbf{V}_x - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \mathbf{V}_y\right).
\]

Thus, the components of the curl are:
\[
\text{curl} \ \mathbf{V} = \frac{\partial}{\partial y} \mathbf{V}_x - \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \mathbf{V}_y.
\]

